$O$ is the centre, and $C$ and $D$ lie on the major arc $AB$. $\angle AOB=166^{\circ}$. Find $\angle ACB$ and $\angle ADB$. Explain why the different positions of $C$ and $D$ do not change the answer.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"geometry","base":[],"semantic":[],"reference":"circle-angle-properties theory.workedExamples[0].question_text; source-supported diagram; ordinary outlines and labels black; no decorative fill"}
\begin{tikzpicture}
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,calc}
\draw (0,0) circle (2);
\coordinate (A) at (187:2);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\coordinate (B) at (353:2);
\node[right] at (B) {$B$};
\coordinate (C) at (65:2);
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\coordinate (D) at (120:2);
\node[above left] at (D) {$D$};
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt) node[above] {$O$};
\draw (O)--(A);
\draw (O)--(B);
\draw (C)--(A);
\draw (C)--(B);
\draw (D)--(A);
\draw (D)--(B);
\pic[draw,"$166^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.55cm,angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle = A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

